<p class="ah-prose-p"><code class="ah-code-inline">to-spec</code> turns the conversation you have just had into a <strong class="ah-prose-strong"><a class="decoration-primary/40 underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-primary" data-state="closed" href="/ai-coding-dictionary/spec">spec</a></strong>, and publishes it to your issue tracker as a single issue.</p>
<p class="ah-prose-p">It does not interview you. When you reach for it, the deciding is already done. So it synthesises what is known (from the thread, the codebase, your <code class="ah-code-inline">GLOSSARY.md</code> and ADRs) and does not start a new round of questions. The spec records decisions you already made. It is not a place to make new ones.</p>
<h2 id="when-to-reach-for-it" class="scroll-mt-[72px] tracking-[-0.025em]"><a class="text-inherit! w-full font-semibold no-underline" href="#when-to-reach-for-it">When to reach for it</a></h2>
<p class="ah-prose-p">You invoke this by typing <code class="ah-code-inline">/to-spec</code>; the <a class="decoration-primary/40 underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-primary" data-state="closed" href="/ai-coding-dictionary/agent">agent</a> won&#x27;t reach for it on its own.</p>
<p class="ah-prose-p">Reach for it when the build is too big for one agent <a class="decoration-primary/40 underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-primary" data-state="closed" href="/ai-coding-dictionary/session">session</a> and must be split across several. That is the whole trigger:</p>
